# Bilbo, Thief in the Night: "Whenever Bilbo attacks, you may cast an artifact, instant, or sorcery spell from your
# graveyard. If an instant or sorcery spell cast this way would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead." Faithless
# Looting on turn 1 draws Sol Ring and Llanowar Elves and discards both. On turn 5 Bilbo attacks and Bot1 casts the Sol
# Ring from the graveyard: it costs {1} less than {1}, so nothing is paid (CR 118.7c: the reduction is of the generic
# part only), and being an artifact it resolves onto the battlefield, not into exile. Faithless Looting (a sorcery that
# is eligible) and the Elves (a creature, which is not) stay in the graveyard.

